# the relocate phase: every relocation of a surviving section is applied to
# the bytes of the output section it landed in
#
# the bytes of every surviving input section are copied to where layout put
# them, the atoms collection dropped cut out, and each kept piece of a merged
# section to its place in its group's block. each relocation then finds its
# row in the set of the output format and architecture by its neutral kind,
# takes its addresses from the layout, the addresses of the GOT slot, PLT entry
# or copy its decision reaches, the thread-local anchors and the index of its
# target's output section from the records that publish them, the index of its
# target from the assign phase where it computes one, and is applied through
# the relocation engine. a relocation the loader binds is left alone, one it
# moves is patched with its static value, and one whose target lies in
# dropped code or has no address in the image is refused, unless it is in
# debug information, which only describes code and is left as it is. a relocation to an index space entry takes the entry's index in the
# output. a function table slot stands for its target, so a reference that
# reaches one takes the slot's address as its target's. an undefined weak
# reference resolves by the format's rule. a reference by a section symbol
# names the byte its addend counts to as the format holds it, so one into a
# merged section reaches that byte of the copy kept for it. a relocation of
# a merged piece is applied only where the piece is kept, the copy that
# holds another piece carrying its own. a relocatable
# output keeps its relocations, so its bytes are copied and not patched.
#
# each slot of a table the format states as holding its target's address is
# written with that address, unless the loader binds it, whose image writer
# encodes the bind. each entry of a table of code is its role's template,
# patched through the pair's relocation rows with its own address and the
# address of the entry it lands in. the address of every loader relocation
# site is filled in last.

